      "title": "L1 — what a WHO publication says",
      "description": "Knowledge-graph layer L1 as a NAMED SUBGRAPH of this layer (owner, 2026-11-13: 'L1..L3 as named subgraphs', after smart-kg's deprecation, issue #359). OPT-IN like cat-harness's `sdlc/`, so that each layer's `tools/` is a tools graph of its own: off in a downstream layer unless it lists `smart-base.smart-base-L1` in its `enableSubgraphs`; this layer enables all six. `L1/graph.json` names what it holds FROM WITHIN: `schemas/` (L1 3.0 and the `l1-library` extension as Zod, the engine every layer uses, and their generated JSON and contexts), and the L1 `skills/`, `processes/`, `tools/` and the `scripts/` those tools run. The layers above, `L2/`, `L2-bpmn/`, `L2-dmn/`, `L3/` and `L4/`, are its siblings and import from it; nothing in L1 imports from them.",
